Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab

Package: homelab-database
Architecture: all
Depends: perl (>= 5.36),
         postgresql,
         postgresql-client
Description: PostgreSQL provisioning substrate for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Installs/configures PostgreSQL itself and idempotently creates the one
 shared `homelab` database every feature's own narrow schema lives
 inside. Ships homelab-bootstrap-app-role, which creates a split pair of
 Postgres roles (a CRUD-only runtime role and a separate CRUD+DDL
 migrate role, both scoped to one schema) for any homelab-* feature,
 using OS-level peer auth only — local `sudo -u postgres`, or the same
 over SSH, or a printed-SQL manual fallback. Never a stored or
 network-transmitted admin Postgres credential.
